:: Suspects {"position":"500,1050","size":"100,100"}
Bramble pulls a crumpled piece of paper out of her apron and smooths it on the table. At the top, in big wobbly letters, it says:

''SUSPECTS (I HAVE A BAD FEELING ABOUT ALL OF THEM)''

"I made a list," she says proudly. "I couldn't sleep. Or sit. Or stop making lists."

[[''Suspect 1: Dracula the vampire'']], he is very old and old people do get a bit crazy. Also wears sunglasses at night, which is a red flag. Would interview.

[[''Suspect 2: Goober the gremlin'']], he screamed for two hours straight on the night of the murder and once ate my doorknob. Would interview. From a distance.

[[''Suspect 3: Mike Wazowski'']], he is TOO friendly. Nobody smiles that much unless they're hiding something. He probably has something up his sleeve. (Does he have sleeves? Check.) Would interview.

[[''Suspect 4: Cornelius the ogre'']], he shouted "You will PAY for this, Hedwig!" in front of the whole town, which is basically a confession with extra steps. Would interview, but bring tissues. He cries.

[[''Suspect 5: Dirk, bigfoot'']], there is Hedwig's blood on his rug (I peeked) and he talks about feet more than is normal. Hedwig made fun of him a LOT. Would interview, but do not look directly at the toes.

[[''Suspect 6: Aurora the yeti'']], she sleeps right next door to Hedwig and the door between them doesn't even lock. Also she is a yeti and yetis are very strong. Would interview, gently. She seems tired.

//P.S. I also have a bad feeling about the squirrel. Would not interview. He bites.//

Bramble beams at you. "Helpful?"

[[Back to the lobby->Hub]]


:: The Pub {"position":"1150,1475","size":"100,100"}
(set: $visitedPub to true)
The pub is called //The Soggy Toadstool//. It's dark and warm, and it smells like beer and wet dog, even though there's no dog. Behind the bar stands Gus, a troll, who has been drying the same glass since you walked in.

"Detective," he says. "Get you something? We've got beer, more beer, and soup. The soup's also a little bit beer."

(link: "Ask about the night before the murder")[Gus puts down the glass. Finally.

"Wild night. First, Goober and Hedwig had a huge fight, right over at that table." He points. "Hedwig said he caught Goober in the council chamber, snooping through the secret election papers. Said he'd report him and Goober would lose his seat. Goober was screaming, Hedwig was hooting, and a chair went flying. I think Goober threw it. Or maybe the chair just left on its own, I don't know."

"And after that?"

"Girls' night! The yetis. Very loud, very fun. Brenda arm-wrestled a moose and won." He picks the glass back up. "Only one strange thing: Aurora drank nothing but water all night. //Aurora!// Usually she drinks more than the moose."

''Notebook: The bartender saw Goober fight Hedwig, and Aurora drank only water at girls' night.'']

[[Back to the search->Search]]


:: The Shore {"position":"1300,1475","size":"100,100"}
(set: $talkedMermaid to true)
The shore is quiet and grey this morning. The waves come and go, as waves do. It's the sea. On a big rock a little way out sits a mermaid with long, shell-tangled hair. This must be Coralina.

She eyes you very suspiciously. "If you've come to tell me to stay away from Dracula, you're too late. The owl already tried. Forty times."

(link: "Ask where Dracula was last night")[Coralina sighs and fiddles with a shell.

"He was here. With me. From three o'clock until almost sunrise, and then he had to run, because, you know." She makes a dramatic gesture, as if she's bursting into flames. "He read me poems. Very bad ones. I loved them."

"All night? He never left?"

"Not for a minute. Ask the crabs, they saw everything. Very nosy, crabs."

A crab nods. Probably. With crabs it's hard to tell.

''Notebook: The mermaid says Dracula was with her all night.'']

[[Back to the search->Search]]


:: Unfortunatelly {"position":"1175,775","size":"100,100"}
You stand up, point, and say the name with total confidence. Very dramatic. Bramble claps a little.

But then the suspect starts explaining. Where they were, who they were with, at what time. Everything fits together perfectly. There are witnesses. One of the witnesses is even a squirrel, which isn't ideal, but still.

Slowly, your finger sinks back down.

The room goes very quiet. Bramble hides her face behind a biscuit.

"Detective," she whispers, "I don't think it was them."

On the other side of the room, someone is humming a happy little tune. Nobody pays any attention.

''UNFORTUNATELY, THE KILLER IS STILL OUT THERE. YOU ACCUSED THE WRONG PERSON.''

Bramble pats your arm. "Don't worry. The sign says //nobody leaves town//, so they're all still here. Allez, let's look again. Properly this time."

(link: "Start over")[(restart:)]
